  "comments": "<p>Coins in iron minted to replace those in bronze, due to metal shortages during and after World War II.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Explanation for the 1942 variant:<br>&nbsp;Type 2A = light iron used on the 2 öre 1917-1919 and 1942.<br>&nbsp;Type 2B = dark iron used on the 2 öre 1942-1950.<br>&nbsp;</p><p><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/6871e493eafa3.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/6871e493eafa3.jpg\"></a></p><p><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/6871e87990dd0.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/6871e87990dd0.jpg\"></a></p><p><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/6871ec7f27f56.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/6871ec7f27f56.jpg\"></a><br>Variant 1949, long / short 9:<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5540ace109121.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5540ace109121.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a></p>",
